    a <ontology/EvidenceQuote/#resource> ;
    rdfs:label "Evidence for Oil Seed used in Varnish, Paint & Lacquer: Andrew Ure, A Dictionary of Arts, Manufactures, and Mines (2nd ed., 1840; Project Gutenberg #44562), s.v. IVORY"@en ;
    <ontology/quoteText/#resource> "Callot’s etching ground for copper plates, is made by dissolving with heat 4 oz. of mastick in 4 oz. of very fine linseed oil; filtering the varnish through a rag, and bottling it for use."@en ;
